  "finding": "ApplyDamageToCard reads getTotalDefense at entry, after receive callbacks, at excess checks/capping and immediately before subtracting. Simulator used raw storage at these positions, causing wrong oldDefense notifications, deductions and spill when callbacks or stored values fall outside0..99.",
  "changes": [
    "Clamp only scalar reads0..99 without rewriting stored defense on nonpositive damage.",
    "Use fresh clamped reads for excess comparison/subtraction/capping and post-callback oldDefense, then store the raw signed subtraction result.",
    "Preserve the initial positive-branch decision and existing destruction snapshot before spill/deal hooks; excess may cap finalDamage to0 without skipping those phases.",
    "Revise four old test expressions that assumed a raw getter; no production change to event routing or corpse handling."
  ],
